<% texl.import "~/lib/tutorial/index.texl" ~> (lib -> bind "tutorial" lib.data) %>
<!--{ ce01 : rich }-->
# 2. Cells

A document is a stack of cells, one per line, as the rows of a spreadsheet.
A cell can hold one sentence or a whole page: its line grows to fit it. You
move between lines and edit them with the keyboard, as in Excel. About five
minutes.
<!--{ ce02 : markdown }-->
## Select and edit

| Keys | What they do |
|------|--------------|
| ↑, ↓, or a click | Select the line above or below, or the one you click |
| Enter, F2, or a double click | Edit the selected line |
| Ctrl+Enter | Keep your changes and leave the line |
| Escape | Throw your changes away and leave the line |

A click on another line keeps your changes too, as in Excel. While you edit,
**Enter** starts a new line of text inside the same cell.

Try it: edit this line, add a word at the end, and press **Ctrl+Enter**.
<!--{ ce03 : rich }-->
## Move lines

The three lines below are in the wrong order. Put them in order:

1. Select the line *First* and press **Alt+↑** until it is above *Third*.
2. Select *Second* and move it with **Alt+↑** or **Alt+↓** until it sits
   between *First* and *Third*.

Each of the three lines holds a hidden step that records its place, so the
check after them sees the order.
<!--{ ce04 : markdown }-->
**Third**<% order = (order ; "") + "3" %>
<!--{ ce05 : markdown }-->
**First**<% order = (order ; "") + "1" %>
<!--{ ce06 : markdown }-->
**Second**<% order = (order ; "") + "2" %>
<!--{ ce07 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (order == "123") %>
<!--{ ce08 : markdown }-->
## Insert, delete, undo

| Keys | What they do |
|------|--------------|
| Alt+Enter | Insert an empty line below |
| Alt+Shift+Enter | Insert an empty line above |
| Delete, Backspace | Delete the selected lines |
| Shift+↑, Shift+↓, Shift+click | Select several lines |
| Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V | Copy, cut and paste lines |
| Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z | Undo and redo |

Try it: select this line, press **Alt+Enter**, press **Enter**, write a
sentence and press **Ctrl+Enter**. Then press **Ctrl+Z** to undo it.

Now delete the line below that says *Delete me*: select it and press
**Delete**.
<!--{ ce09 : markdown }-->
**Delete me.**<% delete_me = TRUE %>
<!--{ ce10 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (delete_me != TRUE) %>
<!--{ ce11 : rich }-->
## Write on an empty line

The numbered lines below the end of a document are empty. Select one, press
**Enter**, write something and press **Ctrl+Enter**: it becomes part of the
document, on that line. Try it below the last line of this lesson.

## Save

Press **Ctrl+S** to save. If you try to leave a document with unsaved
changes, the browser asks you first. Save now, so that the
[index](index.texl) counts your checks.

More in the manual: [Lines and cells](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/lines.html).
